* The SOUND field holds the function name as a string.
* APPLY resolves that name at runtime and passes P as the argument declared by BARK(PETOBJ).
* The selected function sets its return value through its own name before RETURN.
    DATA('PET(SOUND)')
    DEFINE('BARK(PETOBJ)')
    P = PET('BARK')
    OUTPUT = APPLY(SOUND(P),P) :(END)
BARK BARK = 'woof' :(RETURN)
END
